  "concept": "The cross-ratio of four collinear points is preserved when those points are projected from any center onto other lines, even when one projected point lies at infinity.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "projection center O shown as a black point at the left with label O",
    "four black projection rays emanating from O, one for each correspondence index 1 through 4",
    "upper projection ray passing through P4, Q4, and R4",
    "middle-upper projection ray passing through P3, Q3, and R3",
    "middle-lower projection ray passing through P2, Q2, and R2",
    "lower projection ray passing through P1 and Q1 and extending toward infinity",
    "magenta transversal line containing P1, P2, P3, and P4",
    "black points P1, P2, P3, and P4 on the P line with serif labels",
    "magenta transversal line containing Q1, Q2, Q3, and Q4",
    "black points Q1, Q2, Q3, and Q4 on the Q line with serif labels",
    "magenta transversal line containing R2, R3, and R4 and extending toward R1 at infinity",
    "black points R2, R3, and R4 on the R line with serif labels",
    "label R1 with right-pointing arrow to infinity symbol",
    "visual indication that the R line is parallel to the lower projection ray, making R1 a point at infinity",
    "cross-ratio formula annotation CR(A1,A2,A3,A4) = (A1A3/A2A3) / (A1A4/A2A4)",
    "live numeric readouts for CR(P1,P2,P3,P4), CR(Q1,Q2,Q3,Q4), and CR(R1,R2,R3,R4)",
